Hi Timi,

Thanks for reporting it to the mailing list. Could you also report your system (Mac or Windows version)? If you are using the latest Mac OS X (Big Sur), you might check if the command line developer tools are correctly installed.

And please check if you can run other models (not just the rdt_happiness model) and just double check - check if Stan is correctly installed (see this link <https://github.com/stan-dev/rstan/wiki/RStan-Getting-Started#example-1-eight-schools>). Also try the latest version in GitHub (e.g., for R; https://github.com/CCS-Lab/hBayesDM/tree/develop/R) and see if this works.

Thanks and please let us know.

